## Two things worth your attention

**Three of the six fatals are false claims about page structure**, and `prosecheck` passes on all three. It reads positional claims against its spec, not against the page manifest. A cheap mechanical gate that doesn't exist would have caught half this wave's fatals.

**~45 of the 54 nonfatals are one class** — "`[F#]` states a one-line consequence of its cited target". That's the wave-4 A10 queue question, now on its fourth wave unanswered. Settling it either licenses ~45 findings a wave as intended, or converts them into a backlog.

